module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChartSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasicoherentCartesianOnAffineCharts
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SmallEtaleModuleImageData
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SmallEtaleModulePullback

/-!
# Fitting ideal sheaves and pullback along a morphism of algebraic spaces

For a morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` of algebraic spaces and an `𝒪_Y`-module `G`, the ideal sheaf on `X`
generated by the inverse image of the `r`-th Fitting ideal sheaf of `G` is the `r`-th Fitting
ideal sheaf of `f^*G`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartDiagramRestrict` is pullback of regular functions along the
  vertical scheme morphism of a diagram of étale charts over `f`, as a ring homomorphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsCartesianOnAffineChartDiagrams` says that over a diagram of affine
  étale charts the sections of `f^*G` are the base change of the sections of `G`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealPullback` is `f^{-1}Fit_r(G) · 𝒪_X`, the smallest sheaf of
  ideals of `𝒪_X` whose sections over the source of every affine chart diagram contain the ideal
  generated by the image of the chartwise Fitting ideal over the target.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealOnChart_modulePullback`: over a diagram of affine étale
  charts the chartwise Fitting ideal of `f^*G` is generated by the image of the chartwise Fitting
  ideal of `G`.
* `fittingIdealPullback_eq_fittingIdeal_of_isCartesianOnAffineChartDiagrams`:
  `f^{-1}Fit_r(G) · 𝒪_X` is `Fit_r(f^*G)`, granted the three inputs listed below.

## Implementation notes

The generators of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealPullback` are the *chartwise* Fitting
ideals of Stacks 07ZA over the affine étale charts of `Y`, not the sections of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdeal`.  The two generate the same ideal sheaf on `Y`, because
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdeal` is by construction the sheaf of ideals generated by the
chartwise ones, and the inverse image of an ideal generated by a family is generated by the
images of that family; the chartwise form is used because it is the form in which the base
change clause of Stacks 07ZA applies directly.

Three inputs are carried as hypotheses here, and all three are available: the statement of
Stacks 0CZ4 with none of them assumed is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealPullback_eq_fittingIdeal` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/FittingIdealPullbackFiniteType.lean`, which discharges
them from quasi-coherence and finite type of `G`.  They are kept as hypotheses in this file
because the modules proving them are downstream of it.

The first is `IsCartesianOnAffineChartDiagrams`, the affine-chart description of `f^*G`: it is
Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) read across `f` rather than across a morphism of charts of one
space, so it is not
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`, which compares two
charts of a single algebraic space; the across-`f` form is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineChartDiagrams_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`.  Only the
existence of some `𝒪_X(U)`-linear equivalence is asked for, not a canonical comparison map,
because the Fitting ideal of a module depends only on its isomorphism class.

The second is `hpb`, quasi-coherence of `f^*G`, which enters through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite` applied on `X`.  It
is Stacks 03GA, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_modulePullback_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite` proves
it for an arbitrary morphism and an arbitrary quasi-coherent module.

The third is `hcov`: that the affine étale charts of `X` which are the source of an affine chart
diagram over `f` whose target carries finite sections of `G` cover every chart of `X`.  An
affine chart of `X` need not map into a single affine chart of `Y`, so this is a statement about
refining charts, and it is the cofinality of the affine chart diagrams, Stacks 03G2, which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.generate_affineChartDiagram_mem_topology` proves; its finiteness clause
is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.moduleFinite_sections_of_isFiniteType`, which turns finite type of
`G` into finiteness of its sections over an affine chart.

The reduction is to the base change clause of Stacks 07ZA for the chart rings directly, rather
than to the scheme-level `AlgebraicGeometry.fittingIdeal_comap` (Stacks 0C3D) that the source
cites: 0C3D is itself that clause applied on the affine opens of a scheme, and the chartwise
Fitting ideals here are indexed by affine étale charts, not by affine opens of one chart.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CZ4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CZ4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C3D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C3D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03G2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03G2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03GA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03GA)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}

/-! ### Base change along a chart diagram -/

/-- Pullback of regular functions along the vertical scheme morphism of a diagram of étale charts
over `f : X ⟶ Y`, as a homomorphism `𝒪_Y(V) →+* 𝒪_X(U)`. -/
noncomputable abbrev chartDiagramRestrict (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 Y.1 f.hom) :
    chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V →+* chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U :=
  (chartDiagramPullback B S hS f d).hom

/-- The `𝒪_Y(V)`-algebra structure on `𝒪_X(U)` given by a chart diagram.  Not an instance: it
depends on the diagram. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def chartDiagramAlgebra (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 Y.1 f.hom) :
    Algebra (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U) :=
  (chartDiagramRestrict B S hS f d).toAlgebra

/-- The structure map of `chartDiagramAlgebra` is `chartDiagramRestrict`. -/
theorem chartDiagramAlgebra_algebraMap (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 Y.1 f.hom) :
    letI := chartDiagramAlgebra B S hS f d
    algebraMap (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U) =
      chartDiagramRestrict B S hS f d := rfl

/-- **The affine-chart description of the pullback of modules.**  Over every diagram of affine
étale charts over `f`, the sections of `f^*G` over the chart of `X` are the base change of the
sections of `G` over the chart of `Y`.

This is Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) read across `f`; only the existence of an `𝒪_X(U)`-linear
equivalence is asked for, because the Fitting ideal of a module depends only on its isomorphism
class. -/
def IsCartesianOnAffineChartDiagrams (f : X ⟶ Y) (G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2) : Prop :=
  ∀ d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 Y.1 f.hom,
    IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj d.U) →
    IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj d.V) →
      letI := chartDiagramAlgebra B S hS f d
      Nonempty (TensorProduct (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U)
          (G.val.obj (op d.V)) ≃ₗ[chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U]
        (((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G).val.obj (op d.U)))

variable {B S hS}

/-- Where the sections of `f^*G` over the chart of `X` are the base change of the sections of `G`
over the chart of `Y`, finiteness of the latter gives finiteness of the former. -/
theorem module_finite_sections_modulePullback {f : X ⟶ Y} {G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2}
    {d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 Y.1 f.hom}
    [Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (G.val.obj (op d.V))]
    (e : letI := chartDiagramAlgebra B S hS f d
      TensorProduct (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U)
          (G.val.obj (op d.V)) ≃ₗ[chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U]
        (((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G).val.obj (op d.U))) :
    Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U)
      (((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G).val.obj (op d.U)) :=
  let := chartDiagramAlgebra B S hS f d
  Module.Finite.equiv e

/-! ### The chartwise Fitting ideal of a pullback -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0CZ4 on one chart diagram.**  Over a diagram of affine étale charts
over `f : X ⟶ Y`, the `r`-th chartwise Fitting ideal of the sections of `f^*G` is the ideal
generated by the image of the `r`-th chartwise Fitting ideal of the sections of `G` under pullback
of regular functions. -/
theorem fittingIdealOnChart_modulePullback {f : X ⟶ Y} {G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2}
    (r : ℕ) {d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 Y.1 f.hom}
    [hfin : Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (G.val.obj (op d.V))]
    (e : letI := chartDiagramAlgebra B S hS f d
      TensorProduct (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U)
          (G.val.obj (op d.V)) ≃ₗ[chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U]
        (((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G).val.obj (op d.U))) :
    letI := module_finite_sections_modulePullback (f := f) (G := G) (d := d) e
    fittingIdealOnChart B S hS X.1 X.2 ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) r d.U =
      Ideal.map (chartDiagramRestrict B S hS f d)
        (fittingIdealOnChart B S hS Y.1 Y.2 G r d.V) := by
  let _ := chartDiagramAlgebra B S hS f d
  let _ := module_finite_sections_modulePullback (f := f) (G := G) (d := d) e
  calc fittingIdealOnChart B S hS X.1 X.2 ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) r d.U
      = _root_.fittingIdeal (R := chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U)
          (M := ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G).val.obj (op d.U)) (r : ℤ) := rfl
    _ = _root_.fittingIdeal (R := chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U)
          (M := TensorProduct (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U)
            (G.val.obj (op d.V))) (r : ℤ) := (fittingIdeal_eq_of_linearEquiv e r).symm
    _ = Ideal.map (algebraMap (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U))
          (_root_.fittingIdeal (R := chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V)
            (M := G.val.obj (op d.V)) (r : ℤ)) :=
        (fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{u, u, u, u} (R := chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V)
          (M := G.val.obj (op d.V))).2.2.1 _ r
    _ = Ideal.map (chartDiagramRestrict B S hS f d)
          (fittingIdealOnChart B S hS Y.1 Y.2 G r d.V) := rfl

/-! ### The inverse-image Fitting ideal sheaf -/

variable (B S hS)

/-- The affine étale charts of `X` which are the source of a diagram of affine étale charts over
`f` on whose target chart the sections of `G` are a finite module, as a presieve. -/
def affineChartDiagramPresieve (f : X ⟶ Y) (G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2)
    (U : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) : Presieve U :=
  fun W _ => IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W) ∧
    ∃ d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 Y.1 f.hom, ∃ _ : d.U = W,
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj d.V) ∧
        Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (G.val.obj (op d.V))

/-- The ideal sheaf `f^{-1}Fit_r(G) · 𝒪_X`: the smallest sheaf of ideals of `𝒪_X` whose sections
over the source chart of every diagram of affine étale charts over `f` contain the ideal generated
by the image of the chartwise Fitting ideal over the target chart. -/
noncomputable def fittingIdealPullback (f : X ⟶ Y) (G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2) (r : ℕ) :
    (SheafOfModules.unit
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O))).Submodule := by
  classical
  exact sInf { J | ∀ d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 Y.1 f.hom,
    IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj d.U) →
    IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj d.V) →
    ∀ (h : Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (G.val.obj (op d.V)))
      (b : chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U),
      b ∈ Ideal.map (chartDiagramRestrict B S hS f d)
          (@fittingIdealOnChart B S hS Y.1 Y.2 G r d.V h) →
        b ∈ J.toSubmodule.obj (op d.U) }

variable {B S hS}

/-- `f^{-1}Fit_r(G) · 𝒪_X` is contained in every sheaf of ideals of `𝒪_X` whose sections over the
source chart of each affine chart diagram contain the image of the chartwise Fitting ideal. -/
theorem fittingIdealPullback_le {f : X ⟶ Y} {G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2} (r : ℕ)
    {J : (SheafOfModules.unit
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O))).Submodule}
    (hJ : ∀ d : ChartDiagram B S hS X.1 Y.1 f.hom,
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj d.U) →
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj d.V) →
      ∀ (h : Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS Y.1 Y.2 d.V) (G.val.obj (op d.V)))
        (b : chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 d.U),
        b ∈ Ideal.map (chartDiagramRestrict B S hS f d)
            (@fittingIdealOnChart B S hS Y.1 Y.2 G r d.V h) →
          b ∈ J.toSubmodule.obj (op d.U)) :
    fittingIdealPullback B S hS f G r ≤ J :=
  sInf_le hJ

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0CZ4, granted its three inputs.**  The ideal sheaf generated by the
inverse image of the `r`-th Fitting ideal sheaf of `G` is the `r`-th Fitting ideal sheaf of
`f^*G`: `f^{-1}Fit_r(G) · 𝒪_X = Fit_r(f^*G)`.

The three hypotheses are all available; see the implementation notes.  The form of the statement
with none of them assumed is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealPullback_eq_fittingIdeal`. -/
theorem fittingIdealPullback_eq_fittingIdeal_of_isCartesianOnAffineChartDiagrams
    {f : X ⟶ Y} {G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2}
    (hG : IsCartesianOnAffineChartDiagrams B S hS f G)
    (hpb : ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G).IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hcov : ∀ U : SmallEtale B S hS X.1,
      Sieve.generate (affineChartDiagramPresieve B S hS f G U) ∈
        SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1 U)
    (r : ℕ) :
    fittingIdealPullback B S hS f G r =
      fittingIdeal B S hS X.1 X.2 ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) r := by
  classical
  have hcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) :=
    isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS X.1 X.2 _ hpb
  refine le_antisymm (fittingIdealPullback_le r fun d hU hV h b hb => ?_) ?_
  · have := h
    obtain ⟨e⟩ := hG d hU hV
    have := module_finite_sections_modulePullback (f := f) (G := G) (d := d) e
    have hb' : b ∈ fittingIdealOnChart B S hS X.1 X.2 ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) r d.U := by
      rwa [fittingIdealOnChart_modulePullback r e]
    exact mem_fittingIdeal_of_mem_fittingIdealOnChart
      ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) r d.U hU b hb'
  · refine fittingIdeal_le ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) r fun V hV b hbfin hb => ?_
    have := hbfin
    refine (SheafOfModules.Submodule.mem_sInf_obj
      (M := SheafOfModules.unit
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
          (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).O))) _ (op V) b).mpr
      fun J hJ => ?_
    have hsub : Sieve.generate (affineChartDiagramPresieve B S hS f G V) ≤
        J.toSubmodule.toSubfunctor.sieveOfSection b := by
      rintro Z g hg
      obtain ⟨W, g', a, ⟨hWaff, d, hdU, hdV, hdfin⟩, rfl⟩ := hg
      subst hdU
      have := hdfin
      obtain ⟨e⟩ := hG d hWaff hdV
      have := module_finite_sections_modulePullback (f := f) (G := G) (d := d) e
      have hres : chartRestrict (hF := X.2) a b ∈
          fittingIdealOnChart B S hS X.1 X.2 ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) r d.U :=
        fittingIdealOnChart_map_le_of_surjective_chartBaseChange
          ((modulePullback B S hS f).obj G) r a (hcart V d.U hV hWaff a).2
          (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hb)
      rw [fittingIdealOnChart_modulePullback r e] at hres
      have hmem : chartRestrict (hF := X.2) a b ∈ J.toSubmodule.obj (op d.U) :=
        hJ d hWaff hdV hdfin _ hres
      have hgoal : chartRestrict (hF := X.2) (g' ≫ a) b ∈ J.toSubmodule.obj (op Z) := by
        rw [chartRestrict_comp]
        exact J.toSubmodule.map_mem g'.op hmem
      exact hgoal
    exact J.isSheaf b (GrothendieckTopology.superset_covering _ hsub (hcov V))

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
